CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 11 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ nested pack expansion in multi-arg template-id folds \(true\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ nested pack expansion in multi-arg template-id folds \(false\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[temp.variadic]/5 + [temp.deduct] + [expr.const]: a constexpr member function
template body that forms an outer template-id with multiple arguments, one of
which is a template-id containing a pack expansion (`And<bc<true>, And<ge<Ts,
Us>...>>::value`), used to fail to fold.  This is the std::tuple constructor
SFINAE shape (`__and_<__constructible<U...>, __not_<__convertible<U...>>>`).
The root cause was the recursive variadic `And` (`And<B1, Bn...> : bc<B1::value
&& And<Bn...>::value>`): during a nested instantiation the enclosing instance's
pack binding `Bn` leaked into the deduction/build of the recursive `And<Bn...>`
step, which then recursed onto itself and could not resolve `::value`.  Fixed by
clearing a pack's recorded arguments when deduction resets the parameters and
when a pack binds to zero elements.  See cpp11_constexpr_recursive_variadic_and
for the minimal header-free reproduction.  Assertions 1-2 prove the nested
expansion folds to the correct value (true and false); assertion 3 (a wrong
value) must FAIL, proving non-vacuity.
